---
layout: base.njk
three: true
seoTitle: "Raffiuddin Mohammed · QA Automation Engineer & Delivery Lead"
description: "Raffiuddin Mohammed, QA automation engineer and delivery lead. Test automation that runs itself for web, iOS and Android, plus live data dashboards that rebuild every day."
---
<section class="hero hero-3d">
  <div class="glow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="hero-text">
  <div class="eyebrow"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ site.role }}</div>
  <h1>Hi, I'm {{ site.shortName }}.<br><span class="grad">I make data you can trust, and see.</span></h1>
  <p class="lede">{{ site.tagline }} Everything on this site is live: it pulls real news data every morning, rebuilds itself, and publishes, with nobody touching it.</p>
  <div class="actions">
    <a class="btn primary" href="#dashboards">Explore the dashboards <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    <a class="btn" href="/about/#for-business">What I can build for you</a>
  </div>
  </div>
  {% if bbc.places and bbc.places.length %}
  <div class="globe-col">
  <figure class="globe" data-globe data-src="places-data" data-dots="/assets/globe-dots.json">
    <figcaption class="globe-cap"><span class="pulse" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="globe-cap-text">Countries in today's BBC headlines · drag to spin</span></figcaption>
  </figure>
  <div class="globe-time" data-globe-time data-history="/data/globe-history.json">
    <label class="gt-row"><span class="gt-k">Travel back in time</span><input type="range" min="0" max="0" value="0" disabled aria-label="Choose a day"><span class="gt-date">Today</span></label>
    <p class="gt-note muted">Loading history…</p>
  </div>
  </div>
  <script type="application/json" id="places-data">{{ bbc.places | json | safe }}</script>
  {% endif %}
</section>

<section aria-label="Today in numbers">
  <div class="grid three">
    <div class="card stat tint-1 reveal">
      <div class="value" data-count>{{ bbc.totalStories | num }}</div>
      <div class="label">BBC stories tracked across {{ bbc.sections.length }} sections</div>
    </div>
    <div class="card stat tint-2 reveal">
      <div class="value" data-count>{% if insights.leader %}{{ insights.leader.last.toFixed(2) }}%{% else %}n/a{% endif %}</div>
      <div class="label">of global news coverage is about <b>{{ insights.leader.label }}</b>, the top topic we track</div>
    </div>
    <div class="card stat tint-3 reveal">
      <div class="value" data-count>{{ hn.stories[0].points | num }}</div>
      <div class="label">points on today's top Hacker News story</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="muted live"><span class="pulse" aria-hidden="true"></span>Live data, last refreshed {{ bbc.updated | when }}</p>
  {% if outages.services %}
  <a class="outage-strip" href="/dashboards/outages/" aria-label="Outage watch: service status">
    <b>Outage watch</b>
    {% for o in outages.services %}{% if o.level != 'ok' %}<span class="os-item lvl-{{ o.level }}"><span class="st-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ o.name }}</span>{% endif %}{% endfor %}
    <span class="muted">{{ (outages.services | atLevel('ok')).length }} of {{ outages.services.length }} services OK · checked {{ outages.checked | when }} →</span>
  </a>
  {% endif %}
</section>

<section class="demo-teaser" aria-label="Test automation demo">
  <div class="demo-mini" data-demo="mini">
    <div class="dm-phone">{% include "demo-phone.njk" %}</div>
    <div class="dm-copy">
      <div class="eyebrow"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>Live demo · Appium</div>
      <h2>Watch a mobile test run itself</h2>
      <p class="muted">An automated test signs in, shops and checks out in a sample app, with no human touching it. This is what I build for web, iOS and Android.</p>
      <div class="term-pane small"><div class="pane-head"><span class="dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>Terminal</div><div class="term-body"></div></div>
      <a class="btn primary" href="/automation/">Learn more: see the code run <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<script src="/assets/automation-demo.js" defer></script>

<section id="dashboards">
  <h2>Dashboards</h2>
  <p class="muted">Updated automatically, with nobody touching them. Get outage alerts as they happen: <a href="/dashboards/outages/feed.xml">subscribe by RSS</a>.</p>
  <div class="grid three">
    <a class="card dash tint-1 reveal" href="/dashboards/global-coverage/">
      <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">🌍</span>
      <h3>What the world is talking about</h3>
      <p class="muted">Share of global news coverage for {{ gdelt.topics.length }} big topics over the last three months, from the GDELT Project.</p>
      <span class="go">Open dashboard →</span>
    </a>
    <a class="card dash tint-2 reveal" href="/dashboards/headlines/">
      <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">📰</span>
      <h3>Today's headlines, by the numbers</h3>
      <p class="muted">Which BBC News sections are busiest, and the words dominating today's headlines.</p>
      <span class="go">Open dashboard →</span>
    </a>
    <a class="card dash tint-3 reveal" href="/dashboards/tech/">
      <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">💻</span>
      <h3>What tech is reading</h3>
      <p class="muted">The most upvoted stories on the Hacker News front page right now.</p>
      <span class="go">Open dashboard →</span>
    </a>
    {% set downNow = [] %}{% for o in outages.services %}{% if o.level != 'ok' %}{% set downNow = (downNow.push(o.name), downNow) %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
    <a class="card dash tint-4 reveal" href="/dashboards/outages/">
      <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">🚨</span>
      <h3>Outage watch</h3>
      <p class="muted">{% if downNow.length %}<b>Right now:</b> {{ downNow | join(', ') }} {{ 'is' if downNow.length == 1 else 'are' }} reporting problems.{% else %}{{ outages.services.length }} major online services, all running normally right now.{% endif %} Checked every 30 minutes.</p>
      <span class="go">Open dashboard →</span>
    </a>
  </div>
  <p class="muted credit">A big thank you to Gabor, whose ideas and feedback helped shape these dashboards.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>How this site runs itself</h2>
  <p class="muted">The same pattern I use for automated test pipelines: scheduled, self-checking, zero cost.</p>
  <ol class="steps colourful">
    <li><b>Schedule</b>A GitHub Action wakes up every morning.</li>
    <li><b>Collect</b>A Node script pulls GDELT, BBC and Hacker News data, with retries and fallbacks. A second job checks 14 service status pages every 30 minutes.</li>
    <li><b>Build</b>Eleventy turns the data into static pages and charts.</li>
    <li><b>Publish</b>GitHub Pages serves it free. If a source is down, yesterday's data stays up.</li>
  </ol>
</section>
